<H1>Medium data</H1>
Search for medium no. = [1067].
<HR>
Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121&#176;C for 15 min.
<HR>
<P><B><FONT SIZE=3>1067&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;FRESHWATER IRON-OXIDIZING BACTERIA MEDIUM-II</FONT></B></P>
Bottom layer: <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> FeS solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=628">628</a>)                    </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;50.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Modified Wolfe's solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=628">628</a>)       </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;50.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Agar, Noble (BD-Difco)                                   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Top layer: <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Modified Wolfe's solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=628">628</a>)        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> L  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace minerals (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=151">151</a>)                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Autoclave both layer solutions.  Shortly after autoclaving, pipette the bottom layer into each culture vessel (typically 5 ml in 60 ml glass vials, use pipette tips that have been cut to enlarge the opening).  The bottom layer is allowed to cool for at least 30 min to ensure its solidification.  <br>
After cooling of the top layer solution, add per liter the following solutions (filter-sterilized): <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace vitamins (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=197">197</a>)                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 8% NaHCO<sub>3</sub> solution                                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.25&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Add the top layer solution in 5 to 6 times the volume of the bottom layer to the culture vessels containing the bottom layer (e.g., 25 to 30 ml in 60 ml glass vials with 5 ml of the bottom layer).  <br>
Then, cap the culture vessels with silicone rubber stoppers, and replace the gas phase with a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v) gas mixture.  <br>
Comment: The medium can be stored in culture vessels for a certain time by capping with butyl rubber stoppers, instead of silicon rubber stoppers and keeping anoxic in the vessels.  Silicone rubber stopper is O<sub>2</sub> permeable and creates a mircoaerophilic condition in the culture vessels.       <br>
